    "checks": [
      "Occupants must be related by blood, adoption or marriage to the occupants of the main house (550-17B(2))",
      "At most two people may live in the accessory dwelling (550-17B(5))",
      "Only in a single-family detached or semidetached dwelling (550-17B(3))",
      "It must share the sewage disposal and water supply of the main house (550-17B(4))",
      "A detached unit must be an existing building converted on the same footprint, and must use the existing driveway. No new driveway (550-17B(1) and (7))",
      "Accessory buildings are capped at 15 ft in height and must be at least 3 ft from the main building (550-40)",
      "Special exception uses 'must meet the development standards for the zoning district' (550-17A). The lot must meet the district lot size for the house type. Table 4-1 has no per-unit lot area for single-family uses. The Board also applies the general criteria in 550-54J",
      "Renting any dwelling unit needs an annual rental dwelling license (417-10, local IPMC 901.1). This applies if a relative pays rent",
      "The definition in 550-56 says relatives by 'blood or adoption'. 550-17B(2), the operative standard, says 'blood, adoption or marriage', so in-laws most likely qualify. The Zoning Hearing Board decides"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Department of Licenses and Inspections, Zoning Officer, https://www.upperdarby.org/zoning. Pending changes: none found on eCode360 for Chapter 550."
